\"name\": \"dev-workspace\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/iwe-org/dev-workspace\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory layer for coding agents built as an Open Knowledge Format (OKF) v0.2 compliant markdown project graph template. Addresses the critical gap where agents excel at writing code but struggle with remembering why decisions were made. Includes structured graph architecture with typed frontmatter, organized directories for product/plans/features/bugs/spec/architecture/releases, and automated setup skill that reads existing codebases. Supports continuous explore-plan-implement-verify-ship workflow loop with IWE CLI tool for graph querying, refactoring, and validation.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-02\",\n    \"category\": \"workspace memory\",\n    \"sources\": [\"GitHub\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"Memory for your coding agent — markdown project graph template\",\n      \"Agents excel at writing code but struggle with remembering why decisions were made\",\n      \"Open Knowledge Format v0.2 compliant\",\n      \"Maintains graph consistency between sessions\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Crap Comment Nuker (ccn)\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/jonhardwick-spec/ccn\",\n    \"description\": \"Interactive comment stripper that safely removes AI-generated comments, dead comments, TODOs, and Co-Authored-By spam from code across 9 languages (JS/TS/TSX, Python, Java, Kotlin, Rust, C, C++). Uses real parsers (Acorn for JS, tree-sitter for others) rather than regex. Primary safety feature: write gate re-parses files after modification and rejects any edit that would move even a single token, ensuring it cannot eat your code. Features color-coded comment categorization, simulurity clustering, --dry-run preview, and .bak backup creation.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-02\",\n    \"category\": \"refactoring tool\",\n    \"sources\": [\"GitHub\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"Interactive comment stripper that cannot eat your code\",\n      \"Uses real parsers rather than regex for safety\",\n      \"Write gate re-parses and rejects token-moving edits\",\n      \"9 languages, one tool\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Benzi\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/shobhitx64/Benzi\",\n    \"description\": \"AI coding agent and harness that compiles codebases into resolved maps before analysis instead of dumping files into context windows. Creates structured maps containing calls, data flow, and references, then navigates with real tools. Supports Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, Java, C#, C++, C, Go, Rust, and Ruby with three-tier truth system (proven/candidate/runtime-observed edges), runtime tracer for real argument values, model-agnostic design supporting Anthropic/OpenAI APIs, persistent per-repo memory, and dual-engine for code and markup. Edits are syntax-gated using real language parsers with auto-revert and blast radius reporting.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-29\",\n    \"category\": \"AI coding CLI\",\n    \"sources\": [\"GitHub\", \"Show HN\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"AI coding agent that doesn't guess — it reads\",\n      \"Compiles codebases into resolved maps before analysis\",\n      \"Indexes the full resolved structure\",\n      \"Beating Claude Code itself on Sonnet\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Bastet Agent OS\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/yamantaka520/Bastet-Agent-OS\",\n    \"description\": \"Local-first control plane for AI-agent teams that orchestrates Claude Code, Codex, Grok, agy, and Hermes into gated workflows with self-healing capabilities. Features stage pipelines (plan→implement→test→review→merge) with four gate types, failed gates routing back to appropriate stages, vendor quota failure handling with auto-resume, per-run metering, append-only audit log, and team memory built on Agent Memory OS. Includes project lifecycle management, Kanban board with real-time WebSocket updates, resource pool with credential storage, and chat-based configuration with Telegram support for inline approvals.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-28\",\n    \"category\": \"workflow agent\",\n    \"sources\": [\"GitHub\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"Local-first control plane for AI-agent teams\",\n      \"Orchestrates Claude Code, Codex, Grok, agy & Hermes into gated workflows\",\n      \"Self-healing workflows that fix their own failures\",\n      \"Per-run metering, audit log, and team memory\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Antigravity CLI VS Code Extension\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/Nuwanthapasindu/antigravity-cli-vs-code-extension\",\n    \"description\": \"VS Code extension that integrates the agy (Antigravity CLI) AI coding assistant directly into the editor environment. Opens agy as a right-side editor panel keeping code visible on left and AI assistant on right, mirroring the UX of Claude Code and Codex extensions. Features Activity Bar icon, right-side terminal, top-right editor button, status bar indicator, keyboard shortcut (Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+A), smart terminal reuse focus, auto-close on /exit, and configurable agy path and launch arguments. Version 0.0.2 added drag-and-drop file support with Shift-key absolute path pasting.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-28\",\n    \"category\": \"IDE integration\",\n    \"sources\": [\"GitHub\", \"VS Code Marketplace\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"VS Code extension for Antigravity CLI (agy)\",\n      \"Opens as right-side panel like Claude Code and Codex\",\n      \"No need to switch to separate terminal window\",\n      \"Drag-and-drop files to add to CLI context\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Ponytail\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/0xwilliamortiz/ponytail-improved\",\n    \"description\": \"AI coding agent skill that prevents over-engineering by implementing a decision ladder forcing agents to evaluate options before writing code: (1) Does this need to exist? (2) Is it already in this repo? (3) Does standard library do it? (4) Does platform do it? (5) Does installed dependency do it? (6) Can it be one line? (7) Only then write minimum. Reports 54% less code generated, 20% cheaper to run, 27% faster execution, and up to 94% less code on tasks where agents typically over-build. Works with Claude Code, Codex, Copilot CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, and others via npm global install with commands like /ponytail [lite|full|ultra|off], /ponytail-review, /ponytail-audit, and /ponytail-debt.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-28\",\n    \"category\": \"AI coding CLI\",\n    \"sources\": [\"GitHub\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"Makes your AI agent think like the laziest senior dev\",\n      \"54% less code generated, 20% cheaper, 27% faster\",\n      \"Decision ladder before writing any code\",\n      \"The best code is the code you never wrote\"\n    ]\n  }\n]\n",
      "numLines": 142,
      "startLine": 1,
      "totalLines": 142
    }
