on, and CI verification automatically, addressing the problem of massive AI-generated PRs that have increased review burden by 91% according to Faros AI research.\",\n    69→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    70→    \"url\": \"https://devin.ai/blog/introducing-pr-stacks\",\n    71→    \"date\": \"2026-07-30\",\n    72→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    73→  },\n    74→  {\n    75→    \"productName\": \"Windsurf\",\n    76→    \"title\": \"Kimi K3 Model Integration\",\n    77→    \"description\": \"The Kimi K3 model launched in both Devin Desktop and Devin CLI. It delivers competitive coding performance on real-world engineering tasks, approaching frontier-level performance by surpassing GPT-5.5 and falling only behind Opus, Fable, and GPT-5.6 Sol. Notably, it's the only open-source model achieving this level of performance.\",\n    78→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    79→    \"url\": \"https://devin.ai/blog/kimi-k3\",\n    80→    \"date\": \"2026-07-27\",\n    81→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    82→  },\n    83→  {\n    84→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n    85→    \"title\": \"Google Workspace Plugins\",\n    86→    \"description\": \"Cursor added Google Workspace plugins, integrating the AI coding environment with Google's productivity tools.\",\n    87→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    88→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/\",\n    89→    \"date\": \"2026-08-03\",\n    90→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    91→  },\n    92→  {\n    93→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n    94→    \"title\": \"Copilot Cloud Agent Reasoning Customization\",\n    95→    \"description\": \"Users can now customize the reasoning level for Copilot cloud agent, allowing more control over AI behavior.\",\n    96→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    97→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/\",\n    98→    \"date\": \"2026-08-03\",\n    99→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   100→  },\n   101→  {\n   102→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   103→    \"title\": \"Enterprise Team Specialization\",\n   104→    \"description\": \"Enterprise team specialization for managed settings was released, providing enhanced team management capabilities.\",\n   105→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   106→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/\",\n   107→    \"date\": \"2026-08-03\",\n   108→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   109→  },\n   110→  {\n   111→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   112→    \"title\": \"Copilot Automations with Comment Triggers\",\n   113→    \"description\": \"Copilot automations can now be triggered with comments, enabling more interactive workflows.\",\n   114→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   115→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/\",\n   116→    \"date\": \"2026-08-03\",\n   117→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   118→  },\n   119→  {\n   120→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n   121→    \"title\": \"iPad Support\",\n   122→    \"description\": \"Cursor is now available on iPad, extending AI coding capabilities to mobile tablet devices.\",\n   123→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   124→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/\",\n   125→    \"date\": \"2026-07-29\",\n   126→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   127→  },\n   128→  {\n   129→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n   130→    \"title\": \"Cursor Start\",\n   131→    \"description\": \"New Cursor Start feature was announced, providing enhanced onboarding and project initialization capabilities.\",\n   132→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   133→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/\",\n   134→    \"date\": \"2026-07-28\",\n   135→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   136→  }\n   137→]\n   138→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n