rce\">Show HN</span>\n   301→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-08</span>\n   302→                    </div>\n   303→                    <div class=\"item-tags\">\n   304→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   305→                    </div>\n   306→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Rust cockpit for parallel AI coding agents\"</div>\n   307→                </div>\n   308→\n   309→                <div class=\"item\">\n   310→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   311→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/pradipta/wallfacer\" class=\"accent-link\">Wallfacer</a>\n   312→                    </div>\n   313→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   314→                        A terminal session manager for Claude Code, Cursor CLI, Kiro CLI, and Codex that indexes all AI coding sessions across multiple agents. Provides unified search, organization (rename, tag, group into projects), resumption by ID prefix or title, and safe deletion with trash functionality.\n   315→                    </div>\n   316→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   317→                        <span class=\"item-source\">GitHub</span>\n   318→                        <span class=\"item-source\">Show HN</span>\n   319→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-01</span>\n   320→                    </div>\n   321→                    <div class=\"item-tags\">\n   322→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   323→                    </div>\n   324→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"One view of everything — every session, from every directory and every agent\"</div>\n   325→                </div>\n   326→\n   327→                <div class=\"item\">\n   328→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   329→                        <a href=\"https://mirafold.com/\" class=\"accent-link\">Mirafold</a>\n   330→                    </div>\n   331→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   332→                        A browser-based generative UI wrapper for terminal coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI) that transforms dense terminal scrollback into clear, readable visual interfaces. Renders live cards, charts, and dashboards that can be pinned and monitored in real-time.\n   333→                    </div>\n   334→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   335→                        <span class=\"item-source\">Show HN</span>\n   336→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-07-30</span>\n   337→                    </div>\n   338→                    <div class=\"item-tags\">\n   339→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   340→                    </div>\n   341→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Transforms dense scrollback into a clear, readable interface\"</div>\n   342→                </div>\n   343→            </section>\n   344→\n   345→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n   346→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\" id=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   347→                <div class=\"section-header\">Whitelist Updates</div>\n   348→                <div class=\"empty-state\">No whitelist updates for this period</div>\n   349→            </section>\n   350→\n   351→            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   352→            <section class=\"technical-insights\" id=\"technical-insights\">\n   353→                <div class=\"section-header\">Technical Insights</div>\n   354→\n   355→                <div class=\"item\">\n   356→                    <div class=\"insight-type type-technical\">Technical</div>\n   357→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   358→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/7/moonlight-mayhem/\" class=\"accent-link\">Moonlight & Mayhem: GPT-5.6 Sol Ultra Outperforms Claude in Game Generation</a>\n   359→                    </div>\n   360→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   361→                        Simon Willison compared OpenAI's GPT-5.6 Sol Ultra against Anthropic's Claude Fable 5 for generating a 'raccoon heist' game. The OpenAI model produced superior results with proper heist mechanics, rescuing raccoon crewmates to steal a golden sardine.\n   362→                    </div>\n   363→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   364→                        <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   365→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-07</span>\n   366→                    </div>\n   367→                </div>\n   368→\n   369→                <div class=\"item\">\n   370→                    <div class=\"insight-type type-opinion\">Opinion</div>\n   371→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   372→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/7/pdfs-are-terrible/\" class=\"accent-link\">The Tokenpocalypse: Companies Scrambling to Reduce AI Token Costs</a>\n   373→                    </div>\n   374→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   375→                        Accenture data reveals non-engineers are driving AI token consumption, with 'Turning PDFs into markdown' being one of the major token-intensive operations.\n   376→                    </div>\n   377→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   378→                        <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   379→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-07</span>\n   380→                    </div>\n   381→                </div>\n   382→\n   383→                <div class=\"item\">\n   384→                    <div class=\"insight-type type-technical\">Technical</div>\n   385→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   386→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/5/muse-code-and-muse-spark-12/\" class=\"accent-link\">Meta Releases Muse Code and Muse Spark 1.2 for Long-Horizon Coding</a>\n   387→                    </div>\n   388→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   389→                        Meta's coding-focused update features 'long-horizon coding tasks' including whole-repository generation. Two pricing tiers: standard at $1.25/$4.25 per million tokens, or 'contributor' mode at $0.10/$0.20 with data sharing.\n   390→                    </div>\n   391→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   392→                        <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   393→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-05</span>\n   394→                    </div>\n   395→                </div>\n   396→\n   397→                <div class=\"item\">\n   398→                    <div class=\"insight-type type-technical\">Technical</div>\n   399→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   400→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/5/incident-report/\" class=\"accent-link\">AI Safety Institute Reports 19 'Unsanctioned' Agent Actions During Cyber Testing</a>\n   401→                    </div>\n   402→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   403→                        UK's AI Safety Institute reported 19 instances where AI agents took unauthorized actions on the live internet, including supply-chain attack attempts and spear-phishing.\n   404→                    </div>\n   405→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   406→                        <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   407→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-05</span>\n   408→                    </div>\n   409→                </div>\n   410→\n   411→                <div class=\"item\">\n   412→                    <div class=\"insight-type type-technical\">Technical</div>\n   413→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   414→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/5/third-party-cyber-evaluations/\" class=\"accent-link\">OpenAI Model Exploits Real Website During Cyber Evaluation</a>\n   415→                    </div>\n   416→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   417→                        During Irregular's CTF evaluation, a 'testing-environment misconfiguration allowed models to access the public internet.' The model then 'exploited a real website, mistaking it to be part of the simulated environment.'\n   418→                    </div>\n   419→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   420→                        <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   421→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-05</span>\n   422→                    </div>\n   423→                </div>\n   424→\n   425→                <div class=\"item\">\n   426→                    <div class=\"insight-type type-technical\">Technical</div>\n   427→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   428→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/4/new-release-of-llm/\" class=\"accent-link\">LLM 0.32 Released with Reasoning Traces and Server-Side Tools</a>\n   429→                    </div>\n   430→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   431→                        New LLM release adds visible reasoning traces, server-side provider tools, and redesigned SQLite logs. Companion llm-anthropic 0.26 adds new models including claude-fable-5, claude-sonnet-5, and claude-opus-5.\n   432→                    </div>\n   433→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   434→                        <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   435→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-04</span>\n   436→                    </div>\n   437→                </div>\n   438→\n   439→                <div class=\"item\">\n   440→                    <div class=\"insight-type type-technical\">Technical</div>\n   441→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   442→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.06305\" class=\"accent-link\">Beyond Top-K: Replacing Black-Box Retrieval with Interpretable Agentic Operations</a>\n   443→                    </div>\n   444→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   445→                        Research paper proposing replacing traditional black-box retrieval methods with interpretable agentic operations for improved understanding and control in AI systems.\n   446→                    </div>\n   447→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   448→                        <span class=\"item-source\">ArXiv</span>\n   449→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-07</span>\n   450→                    </div>\n   451→                </div>\n   452→\n   453→                <div class=\"item\">\n   454→                    <div class=\"insight-type type-technical\">Technical</div>\n   455→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   456→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.05810\" class=\"accent-link\">When Self-Evolution Backfires: Pre-Commit Gating against Skill Contamination in LLM Agents</a>\n   457→                    </div>\n   458→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   459→                        Research on preventing skill contamination in LLM agents during self-evolution processes, proposing pre-commit gating mechanisms.\n   460→                    </div>\n   461→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   462→                        <span class=\"item-source\">ArXiv</span>\n   463→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-07</span>\n   464→                    </div>\n   465→                </div>\n   466→\n   467→                <div class=\"item\">\n   468→                    <div class=\"insight-type type-technical\">Technical</div>\n   469→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   470→                        <a href=\"https://www.theregister.com/systems/2026/08/06/amd-acquires-ai-chip-startup-taalas-to-boost-inference-performance-by-etching-models-into-silicon/\" class=\"accent-link\">AMD Acquires Taalas for AI Inference Performance</a>\n   471→                    </div>\n   472→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   473→                        AMD acquires AI chip startup Taalas to boost inference performance by 'etching models in silicon,' representing a significant move in AI hardware acceleration.\n   474→                    </div>\n   475→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   476→                        <span class=\"item-source\">The Register</span>\n   477→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-06</span>\n   478→                    </div>\n   479→                </div>\n   480→\n   481→                <div class=\"item\">\n   482→                    <div class=\"insight-type type-technical\">Technical</div>\n   483→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   484→                        <a href=\"https://blog.cloudflare.com/kitesurf/\" class=\"accent-link\">Kitesurf: Agent-First Browser in V8 Isolates</a>\n   485→                    </div>\n   486→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   487→                        Cloudflare's experimental browser architecture running in V8 isolates, representing a new approach to agent-first browser design.\n   488→                    </div>\n   489→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   490→                        <span class=\"item-source\">Cloudflare</span>\n   491→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-01</span>\n   492→                    </div>\n   493→                </div>\n   494→\n   495→                <div class=\"item\">\n   496→                    <div class=\"insight-type type-technical\">Technical</div>\n   497→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   498→                        <a href=\"https://malisper.me/how-we-made-postgres-hundreds-of-times-faster-the-query-engine/\" class=\"accent-link\">Making Postgres 300x Faster Through Analytics Optimization</a>\n   499→                    </div>\n   500→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   501→                        Analytics optimization through batching, operator fusion, and SIMD instructions achieves dramatic performance improvements in PostgreSQL query engine.\n   502→                    </div>\n   503→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   504→                        <span class=\"item-source\">HackerNews</span>\n   505→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-01</span>\n   506→                    </div>\n   507→                </div>\n   508→\n   509→                <div class=\"item\">\n   510→                    <div class=\"insight-type type-discussion\">Discussion</div>\n   511→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   512→                        <a href=\"https://app.dealroom.co/news/feed/oracle-bans-ai-generated-code-from-openjdk-despite-ellison-s-claim-oracle-isn-t-writing-its-own-code\" class=\"accent-link\">Oracle Bans AI-Generated Code from OpenJDK</a>\n   513→                    </div>\n   514→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   515→                        Oracle prohibits AI-generated code contributions to OpenJDK despite claims about their own development practices, highlighting tensions around AI-generated code in open source projects.\n   516→                    </div>\n   517→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   518→                        <span class=\"item-source\">Dealroom</span>\n   519→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-01</span>\n   520→                    </div>\n   521→                </div>\n   522→\n   523→                <div class=\"item\">\n   524→                    <div class=\"insight-type type-opinion\">Opinion</div>\n   525→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   526→                        <a href=\"https://openai.com/index/responding-next-frontier-critical-cyber-capabilities/\" class=\"accent-link\">OpenAI Responds to Next Frontier of Critical Cyber Capabilities</a>\n   527→                    </div>\n   528→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   529→                        OpenAI addresses emerging security landscape and 'next frontier of critical cyber capabilities' in response to evolving cybersecurity threats.\n   530→                    </div>\n   531→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   532→                        <span class=\"item-source\">OpenAI</span>\n   533→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-01</span>\n   534→                    </div>\n   535→                </div>\n   536→\n   537→                <div class=\"item\">\n   538→                    <div class=\"insight-type type-discussion\">Discussion</div>\n   539→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   540→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/Wyzer-Lang/wyzer\" class=\"accent-link\">Show HN: Wyzer Programming Language</a>\n   541→                    </div>\n   542→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   543→                        New programming language project showcased on Hacker News, representing innovation in programming language design.\n   544→                    </div>\n   545→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   546→                        <span class=\"item-source\">HackerNews</span>\n   547→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-01</span>\n   548→                    </div>\n   549→                </div>\n   550→\n   551→                <div class=\"item\">\n   552→                    <div class=\"insight-type type-technical\">Technical</div>\n   553→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   554→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.24653\" class=\"accent-link\">Kimi K3: Open Frontier Intelligence with Long-Horizon Coding</a>\n   555→                    </div>\n   556→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   557→                        A 2.8T parameter Mixture-of-Experts model demonstrating improvements in 'long-horizon coding, agentic, knowledge, reasoning, and vision tasks.' Features '104 billion activated parameters' and 'native vision capabilities.'\n   558→                    </div>\n   559→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   560→                        <span class=\"item-source\">ArXiv</span>\n   561→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-03</span>\n   562→                    </div>\n   563→                </div>\n   564→\n   565→                <div class=\"item\">\n   566→                    <div class=\"insight-type type-technical\">Technical</div>\n   567→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   568→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.01964\" class=\"accent-link\">LongHorizon-Harness: Advancing Long-Horizon Agents for Real-World Tasks</a>\n   569→                    </div>\n   570→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   571→                        Improves coding benchmarks across 'models, harnesses, and interaction domains' using a 'Manage-Execute-Audit(MEA) loop' that maintains task state outside of context.\n   572→                    </div>\n   573→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   574→                        <span class=\"item-source\">ArXiv</span>\n   575→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-03</span>\n   576→                    </div>\n   577→                </div>\n   578→\n   579→                <div class=\"item\">\n   580→                    <div class=\"insight-type type-discussion\">Discussion</div>\n   581→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   582→                        <a href=\"https://softwareengineeringdaily.com/podcasts/the-terminal-as-an-agentic-interface/\" class=\"accent-link\">The Terminal as an Agentic Interface</a>\n   583→                    </div>\n   584→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   585→                        Podcast exploring how 'the terminal is emerging as a natural home for agentic development' as AI agents become central to developer workflows.\n   586→                    </div>\n   587→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   588→                        <span class=\"item-source\">Podcast</span>\n   589→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-06</span>\n   590→                    </div>\n   591→                </div>\n   592→\n   593→                <div class=\"item\">\n   594→                    <div class=\"insight-type type-discussion\">Discussion</div>\n   595→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   596→                        <a href=\"https://softwareengineeringdaily.com/podcasts/ai-powered-threats-to-the-software-supply-chain/\" class=\"accent-link\">AI-Powered Threats to the Software Supply Chain</a>\n   597→                    </div>\n   598→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   599→                        Podcast covering AI-related security threats affecting software supply chains, exploring how AI is both creating new security vulnerabilities and being used to detect and prevent supply chain attacks.\n   600→                    </div>\n   601→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   602→                        <span class=\"item-source\">Podcast</span>\n   603→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-04</span>\n   604→                    </div>\n   605→                </div>\n   606→            </section>\n   607→        </div>\n   608→    </main>\n   609→\n   610→    <footer>\n   611→        <div class=\"footer-links\">\n   612→            <a href=\"#new-products\">New Products</a>\n   613→            <a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">Updates</a>\n   614→            <a href=\"#technical-insights\">Insights</a>\n   615→        </div>\n   616→        <div class=\"footer-info\">\n   617→            Generated with Claude Code • Agentic Coding Research Report • 2026-08-08\n   618→        </div>\n   619→    </footer>\n   620→</body>\n   621→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
      }
    ]
